win32u: hold a resized layered window's new surface without valid rects

The resize hold keeps a grown top-level's new surface back until the window has
painted, but it was only set when bits were copied in. SWP_NOCOPYBITS leaves
valid_rects NULL, and the new surface then holds nothing at all. Windows retains a
layered window's contents across a resize; Photoshop resizes a floating panel, a
layered window, this way, so each step could show the panel's grey background
before its contents.

Hold layered windows there too. Not all windows: that also changed how Premiere's
main window maps at startup. NEUTRON_RESIZE_HOLD_LAYERED=0 turns it off.

--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -3024,6 +3024,21 @@
  * copied one. Windows never shows a resized window blank: the contents follow the window. Lightroom Classic's Masks
  * panel resizes three times per Select Subject, and frame dumps show a whole-panel blank frame each time.
  * Copy first, then update the shape (and flush). Kill switch NEUTRON_COPY_BEFORE_SHAPE=0. */
+/* NEUTRON: SWP_NOCOPYBITS leaves valid_rects NULL, so nothing is copied into the new surface and the hold was
+ * not set. Windows retains a layered window's contents across a resize. Photoshop resizes a floating panel,
+ * a layered window, this way, and each step showed the panel's grey background before its contents.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_RESIZE_HOLD_LAYERED=0. */
+static BOOL neutron_resize_hold_layered(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_RESIZE_HOLD_LAYERED" );
+        on = !(e && e[0] == '0');
+    }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static BOOL neutron_region_after_lock(void)
 {
     static int on = -1;
@@ -3182,7 +3197,8 @@
     {
         /* NEUTRON resize hold: a top-level that GREW onto a new surface is not shown at its new size until it
          * has painted (see neutron_resize_hold_set in dce.c). Set before anything below can flush it. */
-        if (!is_child && new_surface && old_surface && new_surface != old_surface && valid_rects &&
+        if (!is_child && new_surface && old_surface && new_surface != old_surface &&
+            (valid_rects || ((win->dwExStyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) && neutron_resize_hold_layered())) &&
             (win->dwStyle & WS_VISIBLE) &&
             (new_rects->window.right - new_rects->window.left > old_rects.window.right - old_rects.window.left ||
              new_rects->window.bottom - new_rects->window.top > old_rects.window.bottom - old_rects.window.top))
